 /* ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
  * Full screen [public issues 2 and 3]
  *
- * Alt+Enter, the maximize button and a double click on the caption turn the window borderless full screen and back. The
- * swap chain keeps the picture's size and the desktop compositor scales it to the window, so the window keeps the
- * picture's shape: dragged by its frame it stays that shape (WM_SIZING); full screen on a monitor of another shape (21:9,
- * 16:10, 4:3) it is the biggest rectangle of the picture's shape, centred over a black window that fills the monitor,
- * instead of a stretched picture. The caption and the frame are not part of the picture: the client area is.
+ * Alt+Enter turns the window borderless full screen and back. The maximize button, a double click on the caption and
+ * Win+Up maximize the window as any window does [GT6 0103] - a player who works in other programs beside the game wants
+ * a maximized window; before, those also went full screen. The swap chain keeps the picture's
+ * size and the desktop compositor scales it to the client area; dragged by its frame the window keeps the picture's
+ * shape (WM_SIZING). A client area of another shape - maximized, or full screen on a 16:10, 21:9 or 4:3 monitor - gets
+ * the picture in that shape with black around it from the present (rsx_live_draw.c, [GT6 0103]). Full screen is ONE
+ * window over the whole monitor: with the picture's window smaller than the monitor and a black window behind it, the
+ * shell did not take the game for a full-screen program, and the taskbar's bottom edge stayed visible as a grey line
+ * under the picture (seen on a 16:10 monitor at 150 % scaling). The caption and the frame are not part of the picture.
  * DXGI's own Alt+Enter would put the flip-model swap chain into exclusive full screen, which nothing here handles (no
  * ResizeBuffers): every Present then failed with DXGI_ERROR_INVALID_CALL and the picture froze while the game went on;
  * rsx_live_draw.c switches that off (DXGI_MWA_NO_ALT_ENTER) and the toggle here is the only one.
@@ -84,26 +88,6 @@ static LRESULT CALLBACK back_wndproc(HWND h, UINT m, WPARAM w, LPARAM l)
     return DefWindowProcA(h, m, w, l);
 }
 
